# Vendored upstream trees keep their bytes exactly as the pinned commit has them.
#
# The digests in `workbench/third_party/<dir>/provenance.json` are the integrity baseline for these
# checkouts, so Git must never rewrite a file on checkout: a normalization would leave the file on
# disk failing its own recorded digest, and a healthy delivered tree would then be reported as
# tampered with. 63 vendored files carry CRLF, so this is not hypothetical.
#
# `-text` alone is what preserves the bytes. Diffing is deliberately left ENABLED: `-diff` would
# make every vendored file render as binary, which is precisely the reviewability this branch
# exists to provide. Upstream's own `MTST_PTHA/.gitattributes` declared `* text=auto`, and because
# an in-tree `.gitattributes` outranks this one, that file was rewritten to `* -text -diff` too.
workbench/third_party/** -text
